Bipartite Graph(undirected graph):-
  A graph is a bipartite graph, if we can create two different sets of nodes such that no two nodes from same set have a edge between them.
                                            OR
  A graph is bipartite if we can color the entire graph with two colors such that no to adjacent nodes have same color.

  By definition we can say that:
    - A linear graph is bipartite naturally.
    - A cyclic graph is bipartite if it has even length cycle.

    Odd length cycle graph is - non bipartite in nature.



  SAFE NODE:-
  anyone who is part of cycle is not a safe node.
  anyone who is leading to cycle is not a safe node.
  REST all are safe nodes.
